    "created_at": "2017-04-11T01:46:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-11T01:46:47Z",
    "body": "The HTML &lt;input> tag uses regular expressions to define the pattern of file names accepted so there's some precedent for this. It would probably look something like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndictionary USBDeviceFilter {\r\n    unsigned short vendorId;\r\n    unsigned short productId;\r\n    octet classCode;\r\n    octet subclassCode;\r\n    octet protocolCode;\r\n    DOMString productNamePattern;\r\n    DOMString manufacturerNamePattern;\r\n    DOMString serialNumberPattern;\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere is no WebIDL type for regular expressions but `requestDevice()` should raise a `TypeError` if the string provided cannot be parsed as a JavaScript regular expression.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
